# ROWERG INTERVALS

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

RowErg Intervals are repeated high-intensity efforts performed on a rowing ergometer to develop whole-body power, aerobic capacity and repeated force production.

Within CAS, they are considered one of the most effective conditioning modalities for developing posterior-chain endurance and whole-body work capacity with relatively low orthopedic stress.

---

# Philosophy

Combat performance depends on the ability to repeatedly generate force through the entire kinetic chain.

The RowErg reinforces synchronized lower-body drive, trunk stiffness and upper-body pulling while producing an exceptional cardiovascular stimulus.

CAS uses RowErg Intervals to improve conditioning without excessive impact.

